}1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." 13194139537075 17592186576411 false] [17592186396176 1074 "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ kx\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is not a linear transformation.\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, only statement “$T$ is **NOT** a linear transformation” is true." 13194139537075 17592186576411 true] [17592186396237 1071 "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix  $\\begin{bmatrix}k & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & k\\end{bmatrix}$ is singular.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." 13194139537075 17592186576411 true] [17592186396237 1071 "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix  $\\begin{bmatrix}k & 0 & 0 \\\\